# Use an opt-in strategy
*

# Add build props
!Directory.Build.props

# Add global json
!global.json

# Add local tools config
!/.config/
!/.config/*.json

# Add paket targets
!/.paket/
!/.paket/Paket.Restore.targets

# Add dependencies file
!paket.dependencies
!paket.lock
!paket.references

# Add solution file
!*.sln

# Add fsharp project files
!*.fsproj

# Add fsharp source files
!*.fs

# Add source files.
# This one line carries the whole tree: Docker's `*` above is filepath.Match and does
# not cross `/`, so nothing under src is excluded by it and no per-project re-include
# is needed. What must stay out is excluded at the end of this file.
!/src/

# Add data folders
# Only the demo cache belongs in the image. The proprietary *.cache files are
# licence-restricted and are bind-mounted onto /app/data/cache at run time.
# The G-Standaard under data/zindex is not copied by the Dockerfile at all.
#
# Re-including a directory re-includes everything under it, so !/data/cache/ on
# its own carries the *.cache files in as well. The last matching pattern wins,
# so the exclusions below come after the re-includes and keep them out.
!/data/
!/data/cache/
!/data/cache/*.demo
!/data/cache/interactions/
!/data/cache/interactions/*.JSON
/data/cache/*.cache
/data/data/
/data/db/
/data/localization/
/data/logs/
/data/sources/
/data/zindex/

# Keep build output and local trees out of the context.
#
# Docker reads the leading `*` differently from git: its `*` is filepath.Match, which
# does not cross `/`, so it only excludes top-level entries. Once `!/src/` above
# re-includes src, NOTHING below it is excluded by default -- unlike .gitignore, where a
# slash-less `*` applies at every depth. The last matching pattern wins, so these
# exclusions must stay at the end of the file, after the `!/src/` re-include.
#
# None of this ever reached the image (Dockerfile's only stage crossing is
# `COPY --from=app-build /workspace/deploy /app`); it only bloated the context.
/src/**/bin/
/src/**/obj/
# npm ci re-installs these in the app-build stage anyway.
/src/**/node_modules/
# Fable .jsx output; `dotnet run bundle` regenerates it (Build.fs `Clean`).
/src/**/output/
# Local scratch and the retired data tree (renamed data -> data_ by the AppPath
# refactor, f8f19359); untracked, nothing reads them.
/src/**/Scratch/
/src/**/data_/
